  "notes": [
    "All integers are big endian. Each control and device entry starts with its type byte.",
    "verified = true: checked against the vendored scrcpy-server v5.0.1 by android/helper/src/test/java/com/genymobile/scrcpy/anmirror/ScrcpyFixturesTest.java. source says where the layout first came from: spike = the 0.1 spike used it against the real v5.0.1 server; memory = written from memory before the check; vendored = from the vendored source.",
    "Touch: pointer_id -2 is the generic finger; width and height are the current video size; pressure is u16 fixed point (65535 = 1.0).",
    "Scroll: hscroll and vscroll are the encoder's input; on the wire they are i16 = clamp(v / 16, -1, 1) x 32768, truncated toward zero (not rounded), clamped to -32768..32767. The server reads i16 / 32768 x 16 (32767 = 16.0), so 0.1 arrives as 204 / 2048 = 0.099609375.",
    "Touch pressure is read as u16 / 65536 (65535 = 1.0); the server's ControlMessage holds both as floats.",
    "Text and clipboard strings: u32 byte length, then UTF-8.",
    "Video stream entries include the dummy byte when dummy_byte is true. A media packet header is u64 (bit 62 config, bit 61 key frame, low 61 bits PTS in microseconds) and u32 payload size; a session packet sets bit 63 and carries the width and height."
  ],
